From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: thisiscamk <100883750+thisiscamk@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Input: apple_z2: Add iPad Air (J72) touchscreen support

The iPad Air (J72) has an N1 controller with the iPad 5's C1F15,1
personality, so it boots through the N1 path: HBPP firmware packets
checked through ATN_ACK, register calibration, the unit's 1024-byte
multi-touch calibration and execute. What differs:

- SPI: every transfer is sent byte-wise at 1 MHz with a 5 us word
  delay, and a transfer only counts when it completed in full;
- power-on: reset held, reference clock, analog then core supply,
  15 ms, the 0x19 0xc1 wake, display sync active, 10 ms, an HBPP NOP,
  reset released, 30 ms;
- boot: HBPP packets are sent once, register reads check the 0x4c39
  reply header and its checksum, the calibration is mandatory, the last
  firmware packet waits 15 ms and execute 100 ms;
- runtime: the controller is polled every 25 ms with tagged EB reads
  of a length reply and then the checksummed report. Its contacts are
  30-byte records validated as a whole before any slot changes, mapped
  through the surface descriptor the controller reports;
- reports 0xaf, 0xac and 0xc8 are checked and set at start, then read
  back as a health check;
- recovery: three bad frames in a row release all contacts and rerun
  the health check, at most six times a minute; contacts that stop
  being reported for 250 ms are released and the controller is stopped.

The J72 power sequence also runs on shutdown, so the controller is
off before the next boot.

[Orchard: from thisiscamk/ipad-air-j72-linux 2a257d6,
 code/current/kernel/0001-j72-installed-kernel-snapshot.patch
 (drivers/input/touchscreen/apple_z2.c, apple_z2_j72.h), which ports
 his measured standalone worker (code/touch/j72_touch_session.c) into
 this driver. Reworked for the final stack: the whole-firmware
 preflight (the firmware recipe pins the file's hash), the exact
 controller version, surface descriptor and panel size checks, the
 refusal of supplies firmware left on and the "halt power operations
 until reboot" state are left out; contacts are mapped through the
 reported surface instead of fixed offsets; the second apple_z2_stop()
 in suspend is dropped.]
